@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `nii-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s72-period-of-allowance`
IMPORT `nii-s335-branches`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-part-d`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-08, its National Insurance Law half: s 72, s 335 and
-- Schedule A1 Part D (version 0.2.0, 2026-10-07).
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-08's NII modules (vendored copies,
-- VENDORED.sha256), and no other row. Exposes numbers, booleans and this row's
-- record of branches. IL-08 declares `A branch of insurance` constructor for
-- constructor as rows IL-04 and IL-05 do (RECONCILE.md, clash N1); here the
-- constructors are IL-08's, and they leave this module only as the fields of
-- `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner`.
--
-- IL-08's NII half has no failing independent finding that the capstone reaches
-- as a wrong number (its INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md):
--   N2 (s 72(c), a child who died) is not reached: no child of the household dies
--      (BRIEF.md);
--   N4 (Part D's day when the day of the month does not exist) is not used here:
--      the capstone takes only Part D's age in months, and row IL-05 computes the
--      day the same way (its fork F19); in the one month the two readings of the
--      day part, IL-05 declines (NOTES.md section 11);
--   the May-2015 floor of s 72 is not reached: the capstone asks about 2026.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-08, National Insurance Law`

§§ `Schedule A1, Part D — a woman's age`

@ref NII Schedule A1 Part D (row IL-08, nii-schedule-a1-part-d.l4)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-08: the age in months Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for a woman born on` `the date of birth` MEANS
    `Schedule A1, Part D — the age in months fixed for a woman born on` `the date of birth`

§§ `Section 335 — the branches in which the earner pays`

-- The earner is an employee (BRIEF.md), so never a housewife under s 238
-- ("שאינה עובדת"); residence and Chapter 11 insurance are the earner record's.
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      s IS AN `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335`
GIVETH A `A person in a contribution period, for section 335`
`IL-08: the earner for section 335, in` h `, with the statuses` s MEANS
    `A person in a contribution period, for section 335` WITH
        `the calendar year of the period`                                          IS h's `the year of the month`
        `an employee or a self-employed person`                                    IS TRUE
        `an Israeli resident`                                                      IS e's `the earner is resident in Israel, under the National Insurance Law`
        `insured under Chapter 11`                                                 IS e's `the earner is insured under Chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`
        `a housewife as defined in section 238`                                    IS FALSE
        `a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`                              IS s's `the earner is a widow pensioner as defined in section 238`
        `insured under Chapter 5`                                                  IS s's `the earner is insured under Chapter 5, work injury`
        `insured under Chapter 6`                                                  IS s's `the earner is insured under Chapter 6, accident injury`
        `insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured in section 158` IS s's `the earner is insured for unemployment, under paragraph (1) of insured in section 158`
        `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`                      IS s's `the earner is a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`
        `an employee insured under Chapter 8`                                      IS s's `the earner is an employee insured under Chapter 8, insolvency`
        `insured under Chapter 9`                                                  IS s's `the earner is insured under Chapter 9, disability`
        `insured for long-term care`                                               IS s's `the earner is insured for long-term care`
    WHERE e MEANS h's `the earner`

@ref NII s 335 (row IL-08, nii-s335-branches.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      s IS AN `IL-07 the earner's insurance statuses, for section 335`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner`
`IL-08: the branches in which contributions are payable for the earner, in` h `, with the statuses` s MEANS
    `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner` WITH
        `contributions are payable for maternity`                                IS `payable` `maternity`
        `contributions are payable for children`                                 IS `payable` `children`
        `contributions are payable for work injury`                              IS `payable` `work injury`
        `contributions are payable for accident injury`                          IS `payable` `accident injury`
        `contributions are payable for unemployment`                             IS `payable` `unemployment`
        `contributions are payable for employees' rights in insolvency proceedings` IS `payable` `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`
        `contributions are payable for disability`                               IS `payable` `disability`
        `contributions are payable for long-term care`                           IS `payable` `long-term care`
        `contributions are payable for senior citizens and survivors`            IS `payable` `senior citizens and survivors`
    WHERE
        `the list`  MEANS `s 335 — the branches for which contributions are payable, for` (`IL-08: the earner for section 335, in` h `, with the statuses` s)
        `payable` b MEANS elem b `the list`

§§ `Section 72 — the months paid for a child`

-- A child of the household: entitlement arose on the day of birth (the earner's
-- own child, in Israel, BRIEF.md); it ceases on the 18th birthday as row IL-06
-- reckons it (the caller passes that day, from the IL-06 adapter), and has not
-- ended if that day is after the month asked about. Every child of the household
-- lived seven days or left the hospital (s 72(b)): the household lists living
-- children. "A child allowance was paid for the child" is read only where the
-- child died (s 72(c)), which none has: given as FALSE, never read.
@ref NII s 72 (row IL-08, nii-s72-period-of-allowance.l4)
GIVEN `the month`             IS A NUMBER
      `the year`              IS A NUMBER
      `the day of birth`      IS A DATE
      `the 18th birthday`     IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-08: section 72 pays the allowance for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for a child born on` `the day of birth` `who turns 18 on` `the 18th birthday` MEANS
    `s 72 — the allowance is paid for month` `the month` `of` `the year` `, for`
        (`An entitlement to the child allowance for a child, for section 72` WITH
            `the day the entitlement arose`                            IS `the day of birth`
            `how it ended`                                             IS
                IF   `the 18th birthday` AT MOST YMD `the year` `the month` (`Days in month` `the month` `the year`)
                THEN `it ceased, other than by the child's death, on` `the 18th birthday`
                ELSE `it has not ended`
            `the child lived at least seven days or left the hospital` IS TRUE
            `a child allowance was paid for the child`                 IS FALSE)
